<title>INDIA: Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill rises to 8.19 pct.</title>
<headline>Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill rises to 8.19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Friday it set a cut-off price of 98 rupees at its weekly auction of 91 day treasury bills held earlier in the day, down from 98.23 rupees at the last auction.</p>
<p>Dealers said the yield was up at 8.19 percent from 7.23 percent at the last auction.</p>
